3
00:01:38.000 --> 00:02:42.000
The following night, 29-year-old Oceanside cab driver Ray Davis pulled up at a downtown taxi stand on Mission Avenue. At 11.10, a customer approached his vehicle and climbed into the back seat. Ray radioed his dispatcher to inform that he'd just picked up a fare and was headed for South Pacific Street. He didn't report back or respond to any further radio communications. After a considerable amount of time had passed with no contact from Ray, his employer notified police. A beach patrol discovered Ray's lifeless body later that morning in an alley off South Pacific Street in the upscale neighborhood of St. Malo. The 11.10 curbside pickup was Ray's last job for Checker Cab Company, his employer of less than four months. At some point during this trip, Ray's passenger pulled out a gun and fired it into the driver's seat, hitting Ray in the back.
第二天晚上，29岁的欧申赛德出租车司机雷·戴维斯将车停在使命大道市中心的出租车候客点。11点10分，一名乘客走近他的车并坐到了后座。雷通过无线电向调度员报告说，他刚接到一名乘客，正前往南太平洋街。他没有再回电，也没有回应任何进一步的无线电呼叫。在与雷失去联系过了相当长一段时间后，他的雇主报警了。当天晚些时候，海滩巡逻队在圣马洛高档社区南太平洋街的一条小巷里发现了雷毫无生气的尸体。11点10分的路边接客是雷在捷克出租车公司（Checker Cab Company）的最后一次出车，他在这家公司工作还不到四个月。在这次行程的某个时刻，雷的乘客掏出一枪，向驾驶座开枪，击中了雷的背部。

4
00:02:42.000 --> 00:03:30.000
The shooter then aimed at Ray's head and pulled the trigger. The third and final bullet punctured the windshield, missing Ray completely. Two 22-caliber long rifle bullets were recovered from Ray's body. Despite their name, long rifle bullets could also be used in handguns. Ray's cab was found abandoned in an alley one and a half miles up the road. It appeared as though his killer had used the vehicle to facilitate a quicker getaway. Police were puzzled by the seemingly motiveless crime. Ray hadn't been robbed. His wallet had been left behind, as had a small amount of change in his shirt pocket.
凶手随后瞄准雷的头部扣动了扳机。第三发也是最后一发子弹击穿了挡风玻璃，完全打偏了。从雷的尸体中取出了两颗22口径长步枪子弹。尽管名字叫长步枪子弹，但它也可以用于手枪。雷的出租车被发现遗弃在前方一英里半的一条小巷里。凶手似乎利用这辆车来加快逃跑速度。这起看似毫无动机的犯罪让警方感到困惑。雷并没有被抢劫。他的钱包被留在了车里，衬衫口袋里还有一些零钱。

5
00:03:30.000 --> 00:04:27.000
Nevertheless, unrelated armed robberies were examined for possible links. None were found. Both evidence and persons of interest were limited. Ray was relatively new to Oceanside, having moved there with his brother just four months earlier. He didn't have the community connections necessary to pat out a suspect list. Most of the individuals questioned were known petty criminals who were quickly ruled out. A fellow cabbie was also looked into, but accusations against him proved baseless. Then, four days after Ray Davis' murder, a second anonymous call was placed to Oceanside PD. Do you remember me calling you and telling you that I was going to pull a real baffling crime? The caller asked.
尽管如此，警方还是对不相关的武装抢劫案进行了调查，以寻找可能的联系。但什么也没有发现。证据和嫌疑人范围都非常有限。雷对欧申赛德来说还比较陌生，四个月前才和兄弟一起搬到那里。他没有列出嫌疑人名单所需的社区人脉。受讯问的大多数人都是众所周知的惯犯，并很快被排除在外。警方还调查了一位同行的出租车司机，但针对他的指控最终被证明毫无根据。接着，在雷·戴维斯遇害四天后，欧申赛德警察局接到了第二个匿名电话。“你还记得我给你打过电话，说我要搞一桩真正令人费解的犯罪吗？”打电话的人问道。

6
00:04:27.000 --> 00:05:33.000
I killed the cab driver and I'm going to get me a bus driver next. Oceanside police took this very seriously. They had kept word of the initial call they received on April 9 under wraps, so they were certain they weren't dealing with a copycat or hoax. The caller had made good on his first threat by murdering Ray Davis, so there was a very real possibility he would follow through with the second. Faced with an unpredictable killer, the city manager gave officials blanket authority to take whatever steps necessary to protect Oceanside's 25 bus drivers. Buses and bus stops were placed under close observation. At night, military police from the nearby Marine Corps Base Camp stood guard over the nervous drivers on the lookout for any suspicious passengers. Four days after the second threat was made, a woman answered her telephone to hear a man warn,
“我杀那个出租车司机，接下来我要干掉一个公交车司机。”欧申赛德警方对此高度重视。他们对4月9日接到的第一通电话的消息保密得很好，因此他们确信这不是恶作剧或模仿犯罪。来电者通过谋杀雷·戴维斯兑现了他的第一个威胁，因此他很有可能会兑现第二个威胁。面对一个不可预测的凶手，城市经理赋予官员全权，采取一切必要措施保护欧申赛德的25名公交车司机。公交车和公交车站受到了密切监视。夜间，来自附近海军陆战队基地营地的宪兵守卫着紧张的司机，寻找任何可疑的乘客。发出第二个威胁四天后，一名女子接听了电话，听到一名男子警告说：

7
00:05:33.000 --> 00:06:39.000
tonight is the night I'm going to kill that bus driver. The caller didn't give his name, but told the woman to relay the message to the police. They listened to her claim, while also being mindful that the case's notoriety would likely appeal to pranksters and attention seekers. The chaos was making headlines across the city, but concerns dissipated when the killer failed to carry out his second threat. As a precaution, two drivers were assigned to all buses that travelled lonely routes, but for the most part, life in Oceanside returned to normal. Eventually, the Ray Davis case went cold. At the time of his death, he was estranged from his wife and had no children. He was close to his brother and mother, but when they died many years later, Ray's senseless murder faded from California's memory.
今晚就是我要杀那个公交车司机的日子。来电者没有透露自己的姓名，但告诉这名女子将这条消息转达给警方。警方听取了她的说法，同时也注意到此案的恶名可能会吸引恶作剧者和寻求关注的人。这场混乱成为了全市各大媒体的头条新闻，但当凶手未能实施他的第二个威胁时，担忧情绪便消散了。作为预防措施，所有行驶在偏僻路线上的公交车都配备了两名司机，但在大多数情况下，欧申赛德的生活恢复了正常。最终，雷·戴维斯一案成了悬案。在他去世时，他与妻子分居且没有孩子。他和兄弟及母亲很亲近，但多年后他们去世时，雷这起毫无意义的谋杀案渐渐淡出了加利福尼亚人的记忆。

8
00:06:39.000 --> 00:08:03.000
Decades later in 2018, local historian Christy Hawthorne donned a pair of white cotton gloves and began flipping through archived newspapers at an Oceanside museum. She had lived in the city since 1983 and harboured a deep passion for preserving its history. Christy was researching the St. Malo area when a three-word front-page headline caught her attention. Written in large, bold letters across a yellowed copy of the Daily Blade Tribune were the words, Local Cabbie Slain. Dated Wednesday, April 11, 1962, the accompanying article detailed the circumstances of Ray Davis's murder. Christy was unfamiliar with the case which had occurred more than half a century earlier. As she read on, her heart beat quickened. A cab driver, a .22 caliber firearm, long rifle ammunition, a city with a water-based name, a waterside crime scene, its proximity to a military base, lack of a motive or suspects, the randomness of the attack, and, most intriguing of all, a cryptic killer who taunted the police.
几十年后的2018年，当地历史学家克里斯蒂·霍桑戴上一副白色纯棉手套，开始翻阅欧申赛德博物馆里存档的报纸。自1983年以来她一直住在该市，并对保护当地历史怀有深厚的热情。克里斯蒂在研究圣马洛地区时，一个占据头版头条的三个字的标题吸引了她的注意。《每日刀锋论坛报》发黄的复印件上用醒目的大写粗体字写着：“当地出租车司机遇害”。文章日期为1962年4月11日星期三，随附的文章详细描述了雷·戴维斯谋杀案的经过。克里斯蒂对这起发生半个多世纪前的案件并不熟悉。随着她继续阅读，她的心跳加快了。一名出租车司机、一把22口径火器、长步枪弹药、一个名字带水的城市、一个水边的犯罪现场、毗邻军事基地、缺乏动机或嫌疑人、袭击的随机性，最引人入胜的是，一个戏弄警察的神秘凶手。

9
00:08:03.000 --> 00:09:47.000
Alarm bells rang in Christy's mind. This seemed all too familiar. Daybreak on Sunday, June 2, 1963, one year after the murder of Ray Davis, near Gaviota, California. The sharp crack of gunshots echoed across the rolling landscape of Santa Barbara County. Three teenagers who were camping alongside Tejiga's Creek were alarmed by the unmistakable noise. It sounded as though the shots were fired just south of their location, where the creek filtered into the Pacific Ocean. There were no subsequent reports of damage or harm. It seemed as if the shooter had been firing for no reason at all. Later that same day, eleven teenagers were enjoying a day of surf and sand at a beach adjacent to Gaviota State Park, just seven miles west of Tejiga's Creek. By mid-afternoon, the teens had made their way back to the secluded spot just off Highway 101, where they'd parked their cars.
克里斯蒂的心中拉响了警报。这一切看起来太熟悉了。1963年6月2日星期日破晓时分，雷·戴维斯谋杀案发生一年后，加利福尼亚州加维奥塔附近。清脆的枪声在圣巴巴拉县起伏的山峦间回荡。三名在特吉加溪旁露营的青少年被这 unmistakably（难以错辨的）声音惊醒。听起来枪声似乎是从他们所在地正南方传来的，那里小溪流入太平洋。没有关于破坏或伤害的后续报告。看起来枪手是在毫无理由地开枪。当天晚些时候，十一名青少年在紧邻加维奥塔州立公园的一处海滩上享受冲浪和沙滩的一天，该海滩位于特吉加溪以西仅七英里处。到了下午中期，这些青少年回到了101高速公路旁他们停车的偏僻地点。

10
00:09:47.000 --> 00:10:58.000
As they huddled around chatting, a loud cracking sound startled them. The noise was accompanied by a high-pitched whir as something small flew right by them. It was a bullet. Another quickly followed. No one was hit, but the teens were left shaken. They never caught sight of the shooter. Two days later, on Tuesday, June 4, eighteen-year-old Robert Dominguez was at the wheel of his family's 1956 Pontiac. Sitting beside him was his childhood sweetheart-turned-fiancé, seventeen-year-old Linda Redwoods. It was a special occasion for the pair. Both were senior students at Lompak High School and were due to graduate later in the week. That Tuesday was a ditch day, an official day off from classes for the graduating seniors. While their peers partied together, Robert and Linda decided to spend their free afternoon at a secluded beach near Gaviota State Park.
正当他们聚在一起聊天时，一声巨响吓了他们一跳。伴随着高亢的呼啸声，有什么小东西从他们身边飞过。是一颗子弹。紧接着又飞来一颗。没有人被击中，但这些青少年受到了惊吓。他们自始至终没有看到枪手的身影。两天后的6月4日星期二，18岁的罗伯特·多明格斯正开着他家的一辆1956年庞蒂亚克汽车。坐在他旁边的是他的青梅竹马兼未婚妻、17岁的琳达·雷德伍德。对这对情侣来说这是一个特殊的日子。两人都是隆波克高中的高年级学生，本该在本周晚些时候毕业。那个星期二是一个逃课日，是毕业班学生的官方放学日。当同龄人们聚在一起狂欢时，罗伯特和琳达决定在加维奥塔州立公园附近的一个偏僻海滩上度过他们自由的下午。

11
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:55.000
Linda had an additional reason to celebrate. Her eighteenth birthday was just three days away. It was around midday when the young couple hit the road for their trip to the coast. They reached Gaviota before continuing another four miles down Highway 101 to a dirt turnout that provided a good spot to pull over. After stripping down to their bathing suits, Robert and Linda crossed the road and began the arduous track down the hill to the beachfront below. Once there, they unraveled a blanket on a small patch of sand and laid down together. With no one else in sight, Robert and Linda believed they had the entire area to themselves. They were wrong. A man suddenly appeared before them.
琳达还有一个值得庆祝的理由。她的18岁生日就在三天后。正午时分，这对年轻的情侣踏上了前往海岸的旅程。他们到达加维奥塔，然后沿101高速公路继续行驶四英里，来到一个适合靠边停车的泥土岔路口。换上泳衣后，罗伯特和琳达穿过马路，开始了通往下方海滩的艰难跋涉。到达那里后，他们在仅有的一小片沙滩上铺开一条毯子，一起躺了下来。放眼望去空无一人，罗伯特和琳达以为整个地方都属于他们自己。他们错了。一个男人突然出现在他们面前。

12
00:11:55.000 --> 00:12:44.000
He handed Linda a piece of rope and ordered that she tie Robert's hands behind his back. Terrified, she did as she was told. She didn't have a choice. The man was holding a gun. Once Robert was under control, the man set about restraining Linda. Before he could loop the rope and pull it tight, he was tackled by Robert, who had managed to wriggle free from his ligature. An altercation ensued. Despite sustaining several bruise-inducing blows to the face, Robert managed to overpower his opponent. He and Linda then ran for their lives. The gunman scrambled to his feet. The two teens hadn't gotten far.
他递给琳达一根绳子，命令她把罗伯特的双手反绑在身后。她吓坏了，只能照做。她别无选择。那个男人手里拿着枪。一旦罗伯特被控制住，那名男子便开始束缚琳达。在他还没来得及把绳子套上并拉紧之前，罗伯特猛扑过去将他扑倒，罗伯特已经设法从捆绑中挣脱了出来。一场搏斗随之展开。尽管面部挨了好几拳并留下了瘀伤，罗伯特还是成功制服了对手。他和琳达随后拼命逃跑。持枪歹徒挣扎着爬起身来。这两个年轻人并没有跑多远。

13
00:12:44.000 --> 00:13:37.000
The only way out was up, and the rugged hillside was slowing their escape. The attacker raised his gun and took aim. He fired over and over until the chamber was empty and his targets had fallen. He reloaded, then marched intently to where his victims lay bleeding in the sand. He then shot them both several more times at close range. Robert was shot 11 times, Linda rate. After the slaughter, the shooter dragged Robert's body 30 feet across the rough terrain to a driftwood shack hidden in the bushes. He pulled Robert inside before collecting Linda and dumping her on top of her boyfriend.
唯一的出路就是往上爬，而崎岖的山坡减慢了他们逃跑的速度。袭击者举起枪瞄准。他一枪接一枪地开枪，直到弹匣打空，他的目标倒下。他重新装弹，然后大步走向他的受害者，他们正躺在沙滩上流血。随后，他在近距离对准他们俩又各开了数枪。罗伯特中弹11次，琳达中弹8次。大屠杀过后，凶手将罗伯特的尸体拖过30英尺崎岖不平的地形，拉到藏在灌木丛中的一个流木窝棚里。他把罗伯特拉了进去，然后把琳达也拖过来，扔在她男朋友的身上。

14
00:13:37.000 --> 00:14:45.000
He then cut Linda's bathing suit open with a knife, exposing her breasts. It was easy to pull down the shack's dilapidated roof to conceal the bodies. After stacking further debris on top, the killer lit several matches and threw them at a tarpaulin covering the shack's entrance. It was time to leave. The fire would take care of the rest. It was nearing 10 o'clock the following night when California Highway Patrol Officer Paul Schultz drove along Highway 101, 22 miles southwest of Lompoc. The area was quiet, save for the sound of the sea crashing against the coastline. Officer Schultz approached a stretch of roadway south of Gaviota State Park, where three men were standing by the side of the road. One was George Dominguez, who was out looking for his son, Robert.
接着，他用刀划开琳达的泳衣，露出了她的胸部。推倒窝棚破旧的屋顶以掩盖尸体是轻而易举的事。在堆积了更多杂物之后，凶手划了几根火柴，扔在覆盖着窝棚入口的防水油布上。是时候离开了。大火会处理剩下的事情。第二天晚上快10点时，加利福尼亚州公路巡逻队警官保罗·舒尔茨沿着101高速公路行驶，位于隆波克西南22英里处。周围一片寂静，只有海浪拍打海岸线的声音。舒尔茨警官接近了加维奥塔州立公园以南的一段公路，三名男子正站在路边。其中一人是乔治·多明格斯，他出来寻找他的儿子罗伯特。

15
00:14:45.000 --> 00:15:35.000
No one had heard from Robert or his fiance Linda since they left for the beach the day before. George Dominguez had gathered a small search party at the teen's last known location. They had since made an important discovery. The men led Officer Schultz to a turnout off the highway. Parked in the dirt by some bushes was the Dominguez family's Pontiac. The doors were locked. Three empty soda bottles were spotted within. Linda's purse lay on the floor in the front, and her and Robert's clothing was strewn about in the back. This confirmed the couple had made it to the beach, but they hadn't returned to the vehicle since.
自从罗伯特和他的未婚妻琳达前一天出发去海滩以来，就再也没有人听到他们的消息。乔治·多明格斯在青少年最后已知的位置召集了一支小型搜救队。此后他们有了重要发现。这几名男子带领舒尔茨警官来到高速公路旁的一个岔路口。多明格斯一家的庞蒂亚克汽车停在灌木丛旁的泥土地里。车门锁着。车内发现三个空苏打水瓶。琳达的手提包落在前排地板上，她和罗伯特的衣服则散落在后座上。这证实了这对情侣确实到了海滩，但之后就没有再回到车里。

16
00:15:35.000 --> 00:16:37.000
One of George's companions informed Officer Schultz that there was a makeshift shack on the nearby beach where local youths were known to hang out. Schultz crossed the highway and headed towards the shore to check if the missing teens were there. It took a few minutes to hike down the steep, bush-lined trail to the water's edge. The secluded area attracted few visitors, aside from drifters who travelled along the nearby Southern Pacific Railroad. One had built the shack out of driftwood, cardboard, tin and grass among the trees and vegetation a few yards back from the water. When Officer Schultz reached the crudely built shack, it was in bad shape. Someone had tried to destroy it by pulling the roof down from within. Inside, partially concealed by the collapsed roof, was a horrific site.
乔治的一位同伴告诉舒尔茨警官，附近海滩上有一个临时搭建的窝棚，当地的年轻人在那里闲逛是出了名的。舒尔茨穿过高速公路，朝海岸走去，查看失踪的青少年是否在那里。沿着陡峭、灌木丛生的山路下行到水边花了几分钟。这处偏僻的地区很少吸引游客，除了沿附近南太平洋铁路出行的流浪汉。其中一人用浮木、硬纸板、锡皮和青草在水边几码外的树木和植被中搭建了这个窝棚。当舒尔茨警官到达这个简陋的窝棚时，它已经破烂不堪。有人曾试图从内部拉倒屋顶来摧毁它。里面是一个可怕的场景，被坍塌的屋顶遮掩了一部分。

17
00:16:37.000 --> 00:17:40.000
The bloody bodies of Robert Dominguez and Linda Redwoods were piled one on top of the other. 22 calibre long rifle bullets, lengths of pre-cut cord and burnt-out matches found throughout the crime scene helped investigators piece together what likely happened. While Linda's bathing suit was cut open, there was no evidence that she had been sexually assaulted. Police were dealing with a particularly cunning offender, who had the foresight to stage the crime scene in an attempt to throw them off. It was clear the killer had hoped to cover up his crime by destroying the shack. But, unluckily for him, the matches snuffed out before the fire took hold. As both victims were popular and well liked, it was hard to identify a motive for the killings. But, not everyone was happy for the young couple.
罗伯特·多明格斯和琳达·雷德伍德血肉模糊的尸体一具叠在另一具上面。现场发现的.22口径长步枪子弹、预先切好的绳索段和烧焦的火柴，帮助调查人员拼凑出了可能发生的事情。虽然琳达的泳衣被割开了，但没有证据表明她遭到过性侵犯。警方面对的是一个格外狡猾的罪犯，他具有远见，试图伪造犯罪现场来误导警方。很明显，凶手希望通过烧毁窝棚来掩盖罪行。但对凶手来说不幸的是，火势蔓延之前火柴就熄灭了。由于两名受害者都很受欢迎且人缘很好，很难确定杀戮的动机。但是，并不是所有人都为这对年轻情侣感到高兴。

18
00:17:40.000 --> 00:18:49.000
17 year old Jason, not his real name, was known to be openly jealous of Robert Dominguez. Robert was a star player on the school's football team and was dating a cheerleader, whereas Jason was in and out of trouble with police. He'd been arrested multiple times, including immediately after the murders for causing trouble while intoxicated. On the day of the double homicide, Jason was at a beach four miles from the one Robert and Linda were visiting. During questioning, police noticed that Jason's hand was bruised as though he'd been in a fight. He also admitted to having access to his father's guns. Still, there was nothing directly linking Jason to the murders, and he was released without charge. After speaking with locals, railroad men and youths that frequented the beach area, investigators became aware of a 50 year old army veteran turned drifter named George Gill.
17岁的杰森（化名）是出了名的公开嫉妒罗伯特·多明格斯。罗伯特是学校橄榄球队的明星球员，还在和一个啦啦队员交往，而杰森则三番两次惹上警察麻烦。他曾多次被捕，包括在谋杀案发生后不久因醉酒滋事而被捕。在双重谋杀案发生的当天，杰森正在距离罗伯特和琳达游玩海滩四英里外的一个海滩上。在接受讯问时，警察注意到杰森的手上有瘀伤，看起来像是打过架。他也承认自己可以接触到他父亲的枪支。尽管如此，没有任何证据直接将杰森与谋杀案联系起来，他在没有被起诉的情况下获释。在与当地人、铁路工人和经常光顾海滩的年轻人交谈后，调查人员注意到了一名50岁、曾当过士兵后流浪的男子，名叫乔治·吉尔。

19
00:18:49.000 --> 00:20:16.000
A loner with a penchant for military style clothing, Gill visited the Gaviota beach often, surviving on the pelicans, mussels and wild mustard he found there. Gill had actually built the shack where Robert and Linda's bodies were found, and was reportedly living in it in the days prior to the murders. He kept a .22 caliber rifle in a bundle strapped to his back, which he was seen firing in the area. Could Gill have been responsible for the gunshots heard and even felt by the two groups of teenagers near Tahiga's Creek and Gaviota State Park in the days before Robert and Linda were killed? The teens had described the gunfire as having come from a .22 caliber semi-automatic firearm, possibly a long rifle. There was no way to know for sure. By the time Gill was brought to police attention, he was long gone. The bullets recovered from Robert and Linda's bodies were too versatile to isolate exactly what type of firearm they came from. But the discovery of several boxes of Winchester-Western Super-X long rifle ammunition inside the beach shack helped direct detectives to the bullet's origin.
吉尔是一个独行侠，偏爱军装风格的服装，经常光顾加维奥塔海滩，靠在那里找到的鹈鹕、贻贝和野芥菜维生。吉尔实际上就是罗伯特和琳达尸体被发现的那个窝棚的建造者，据报道在谋杀案发生前的几天里他一直住在里面。他背上绑着一个包裹，里面藏着一把.22口径步枪，有人看到他在该地区开枪。吉尔会不会是罗伯特和琳达遇害前几天在特吉加溪和加维奥塔州立公园附近的两群青少年听到甚至感受到枪声的罪魁祸首？青少年们曾将枪声描述为来自一把.22口径半自动火器，很可能是一支长步枪。没有办法确切知道了。当吉尔进入警方视线时，他早已不知所踪。从罗伯特和琳达尸体中取出的子弹具有极高的通用性，无法明确锁定它们来自哪种特定火器。但海滩窝棚内发现的几盒温彻斯特-西部超级X（Winchester-Western Super-X）长步枪弹药帮助侦探锁定了子弹的来源。

20
00:20:16.000 --> 00:21:49.000
The boxes, one empty and three partially filled, featured a lot number, TL-21. While this batch was stocked in local sports stores, it was also sold at a base exchange at the Vandenberg Air Force Base, just over 9 miles from Lompoc. Yet, the boxes lacked any identifiers that could help narrow down where or when they were purchased. As these bullets were also the most popular and common type of ammunition purchased, it was difficult to isolate a suspect using this evidence alone. The graduation ceremony for Lompoc High's senior class of 1963 was held on Thursday June 6, the day after Robert Dominguez and Linda Edwards were found murdered. The mood amongst the students was somber, and they laid wreaths on two empty seats in honor of their slain classmates. That same day, two teens were transferred to Santa Barbara County Sheriff's Department, having just confessed to witnessing a murder. Daytime on Friday May 31, 1963, four days before the murders of Robert Dominguez and Linda Edwards, in Santa Cruz, California.
这些盒子，一个空的，三个半满，上面印有一个批号：TL-21。虽然这批货物在当地的体育用品商店有售，但它也在距离隆波克仅9英里多一点的范登堡空军基地的基地小卖部出售。然而，这些盒子上没有任何标识可以帮助缩小购买地点或时间的范围。由于这些子弹也是购买量最大、最常见的弹药类型，仅凭这一证据很难孤立出嫌疑人。1963届隆波克高中高年级毕业典礼于6月6日星期四举行，也就是罗伯特·多明格斯和琳达·爱德华兹被发现遇害的第二天。学生们的情绪十分低落，他们为了纪念被害的同班同学，在两个空座位上摆放了花圈。同一天，两名青少年被移交给圣巴巴拉县警长办公室，他们刚刚承认目击了一场谋杀。1963年5月31日星期五白天，在罗伯特·多明格斯和琳达·爱德华兹谋杀案发生四天前，地点加利福尼亚州圣克鲁斯。

21
00:21:49.000 --> 00:23:04.000
16-year-old James Coleman and his friend, 17-year-old JC Reed Jr., eyed the stranger before them. He was maybe a year or two older than them, of average height and build, with thick natural blonde hair combed to one side. A pair of black-rimmed prescription eyeglasses framed his pale blue eyes. In between taking drags from a pal-mouthed cigarette he held at the base of his fingers, the stranger introduced himself as Sandy and said he'd run away from his home in San Francisco. Sandy's story was inconsistent. Each time he told it, the details varied slightly. Whatever the truth, Sandy was a transient who'd taken to sleeping under the Santa Cruz boardwalk. His peculiarities soon made him a recognizable figure to locals, who thought his army fatigues were an odd choice of attire for someone living on the beach. Sandy often asked other young men where he could find girls, even though girls clearly weren't interested in him.
16岁的詹姆斯·科尔曼和他的朋友、17岁的J·C·里德二世打量着眼前的陌生人。他可能比他们大一两岁，中等身高和身材，浓密的天然金发梳向一边。一副黑框处方眼镜框住了他苍白蓝色的眼睛。在一边抽着夹在指根处的一支平口香烟的同时，陌生人自我介绍叫桑迪，并说他是从旧金山的家中逃出来的。桑迪的故事前后矛盾。每次他讲述时，细节都会略有不同。不管真相如何，桑迪是一个开始睡在圣克鲁斯木栈道底下的流浪汉。他的古怪之处很快使他成为当地人熟悉的人物，他们认为他穿的军服对于一个住在海滩上的人来说是一个奇怪的选择。桑迪经常问其他年轻男子他在哪里可以找到女孩，尽管女孩们显然对毫无兴趣。

22
00:23:04.000 --> 00:24:17.000
On one occasion, Sandy received a warning from police after a young woman complained that he'd been bothering her. While Sandy's requests for food or drinks from passers-by weren't particularly unusual, he raised eyebrows when he produced a knife and asked where he could get it sharpened. There was no doubt that Sandy was a strange character, but James Coleman and JC Reed Jr. were somewhat charmed by him. On the day they met, the trio teamed up and embarked on a crime spree that led them 200 miles south to Lompoc. Coleman and Reed weren't new to petty crime, but Sandy's influence seemingly emboldened them to commit increasingly violent acts. First, they stole some drinks from a YMCA, then they robbed a woman of $20. Next, they stole a sunbeam convertible. During their misadventures, Coleman and Reed gifted Sandy a pair of black pants and a black slip-over shirt with a button-down collar.
有一次，一名年轻女子抱怨桑迪一直在纠缠她后，桑迪收到了警方的警告。虽然桑迪向路人索要食物或饮料并不算特别寻常，但当他掏出一把刀并询问哪里可以把它磨锋利时，他还是让人侧目。毫无疑问，桑迪是一个奇怪的角色，但詹姆斯·科尔曼和J·C·里德二世在某种程度上被他吸引了。在他们相遇的那天，三人一拍即合，开始了一场犯罪狂欢，一路向南200英里来到了隆波克。科尔曼和里德对轻微犯罪并不陌生，但桑迪的影响似乎助长了他们犯下越来越暴力的行为。首先，他们从基督教青年会偷了一些饮料，然后他们抢劫了一名妇女20美元。接下来，他们偷了一辆阳光牌敞篷车。在他们的胡闹期间，科尔曼和里德送给桑迪一条黑裤子和一个带有纽扣领的黑色套头衫。

23
00:24:17.000 --> 00:25:05.000
They also supplied him with a yellow-handled fishing knife, though Sandy desired a deadlier weapon. He kept talking about wanting to procure a .22 caliber rifle. In Lompoc later that night, they approached 63-year-old quarry worker Vernon Smith with the intention of robbing him. Sandy asked for Vernon's help, explaining that they'd run out of gas. As Vernon used a gas can to fill the tank of the stolen sunbeam, Sandy walked up behind him and pulled out his fishing knife. This wasn't part of the plan. Coleman yelled at Sandy. Don't do it, boy.
他们还给他提供了一把黄柄钓鱼刀，尽管桑迪渴望得到更致命的武器。他一直喋喋不休地谈论着想要弄到一把.22口径步枪。当天晚些时候在隆波克，他们接近了63岁的采石场工人弗农·史密斯，企图抢劫他。桑迪请求弗农帮忙，解释说他们的汽油用完了。当弗农用油桶给偷来的阳光牌汽车加油时，桑迪走到他身后拔出了他的钓鱼刀。这不是计划的一部分。科尔曼向桑迪大喊。别这么做，伙计。

24
00:25:05.000 --> 00:26:05.000
Sandy ignored him and plunged the knife into Vernon's back, killing him. Stunned by the sudden and brutal attack, Coleman asked Sandy why he did it. Sandy shrugged and with cool indifference said he didn't know. He then laughed as if the whole thing was a joke. The murder marked the end of Sandy's time with Coleman and Reid. Unnerved, the boys ditched Sandy at a motel in a Royal Grande, 45 miles north of Lompoc. The very next day, Robert Dominguez and Linda Edwards were shot dead on Gaviota Beach. Police caught up with the James Coleman and JC Reid Jr. and arrested them in relation to one of the robberies they committed during their crime spree.
桑迪不理睬他，把刀刺进弗农的背部，杀死了他。面对突如其来的残酷袭击，科尔曼感到震惊，他问桑迪为什么要这么做。桑迪耸了耸肩，冷漠地说他不知道。然后他大笑起来，好像整件事只是个笑话。这起谋杀标志着桑迪与科尔曼和里德的相处时间的结束。感到不安的男孩们在距离隆波克以北45英里的阿罗约格兰德的一家汽车旅馆抛弃了桑迪。就在第二天，罗伯特·多明格斯和琳达·爱德华兹在加维奥塔海滩被枪杀。警方追查到詹姆斯·科尔曼和J·C·里德二世，并因他们在此次犯罪狂欢中犯下的其中一起抢劫案而将其逮捕。

25
00:26:05.000 --> 00:27:06.000
When grilled about Vernon Smith's murder, the pair quickly implicated Sandy, but neither could provide his full name. They weren't even certain if he was really named Sandy. While police were wary of Coleman and Reid's story, it appeared to be the truth. Other people confirmed Sandy's existence and he had been sighted with Coleman and Reid in Lompoc. One witness recalled him carrying a yellow-handled fishing knife, exactly like the one Coleman and Reid said he used to kill Vernon Smith. There had been no sightings of Sandy since Coleman and Reid abandoned him at the motel in a Royal Grande, but police were able to piece together his possible movements. After killing Vernon Smith, Sandy had pocketed $20. It was believed that he used some of this money to fund an overnight stay at the motel.
当被严厉审问关于弗农·史密斯的谋杀案时，两人很快供出了桑迪，但谁也说不出他的全名。他们甚至不确定他是不是真的叫桑迪。虽然警方对科尔曼和里德的说法持警惕态度，但它似乎是事实。其他人证实了桑迪的存在，并且有人看到他与科尔曼和里德在隆波克出现过。一名目击者回忆说他带着一把黄柄钓鱼刀，正如科尔曼和里德所说他用来杀死弗农·史密斯的那把一模一样。自从科尔曼和里德在阿罗约格兰德的汽车旅馆抛弃桑迪以来，就再也没有人见过他，但警方能够拼凑出他可能的动向。杀死弗农·史密斯后，桑迪口袋里揣着20美元。据信他用这部分钱资助了在汽车旅馆过夜的费用。

26
00:27:06.000 --> 00:28:08.000
He booked a room using the pseudonym William Carr and a fake address before checking out at 11 the following morning. A seasoned hitchhiker, Sandy would have been capable of securing a ride further south. He could have obtained a gun and ammunition at any point throughout his journey. Known for approaching locals and begging for help, someone might have told him he could stay at the beach shack near Gabiota State Park. No stranger to sleeping rough, Sandy would have been comfortable hold up there for a night. He might have spotted Robert Dominguez and Linda Redwoods arriving the next day. Sandy was carrying at least one knife which he could have used to cut the rope ligatures as well as Linda's bathing suit. Given he was a smoker, it was likely he would have been carrying a pack of matches.
他使用威廉·卡尔（William Carr）这个化名和假地址登记了一个房间，然后在第二天早上11点退房。作为一名经验丰富的搭便车者，桑迪有能力搭车去更南边的地方。他本可以在旅途中的任何时候获取枪支和弹药。由于众所周知他会接近当地人并乞求帮助，可能有人告诉他可以住在加维奥塔州立公园附近的海滩窝棚里。对露宿并不陌生的桑迪，在那里安顿一晚会觉得很舒适。他可能在第二天发现罗伯特·多明格斯和琳达·雷德伍德到达。桑迪随身携带至少一把刀，他可以用它来割断绳索以及琳达的泳衣。鉴于他是个烟民，他很可能随身携带一包火柴。

27
00:28:08.000 --> 00:29:08.000
This timeline, coupled with Sandy's willingness to kill and desire to obtain a .22 caliber firearm, put him high on the list of suspects in the double homicide. The hunt for Sandy was on. A composite sketch was created based on descriptions from those who had interacted with him. Police dubbed him the laughing boy and the laughing killer due to his amused demeanor following the stabbing of Vernon Smith. Alleged sightings of Sandy were reported across the state. Sacramento teen Robert Lee Bell was one such lookalike. The 17-year-old raised eyebrows when he abruptly quit his job at a Lompoc car wash and skipped town days before the Dominguez-Edwards murders. Before he left, he stole a .22 caliber rifle and ammunition.
这个时间线，加上桑迪杀人的意愿和获得.22口径火器的渴望，使他在这起双重谋杀案的嫌疑人名单中名列前茅。对桑迪的搜捕随即展开。根据与他有过接触的人的描述，警方制作了一张合成素描。由于他在刺死弗农·史密斯后表现出的愉悦神态，警方给他起了个绰号叫“爱笑的男孩”和“爱笑的杀手”。全州各地都有人报告说疑似看到了桑迪。萨克拉门托少年罗伯特·李·贝尔就是这样一个相貌相似的人。这名17岁的少年在多明格斯-爱德华兹谋杀案发生的几天前，突然辞去了隆波克洗车场的工作并逃离了该镇，这让人感到意外。在他离开之前，他偷了一把.22口径步枪和弹药。

28
00:29:08.000 --> 00:30:11.000
When police tracked Bell down, he still had the gun in his possession. Week-old scratches marked his wrists and forearms, but Bell insisted they'd been caused by a puppy. Ballistics confirmed that Bell's rifle wasn't the murder weapon, and when several witnesses placed him at a Sacramento baseball game on the day of the shooting, he was dropped as a suspect. Bell was just one of several young men suspected of being Sandy. While some owned or had access to .22 caliber firearms, investigators couldn't connect any of these weapons to the crime. Clues were scarce, and those police did have were confusing. Sandy had left behind a green military jacket, which had the name Robert Kaufman scrawled along the inside of the collar. Coleman and Reid recalled Sandy saying he had stolen the jacket and the rest of his army clothes.
当警察追踪到贝尔时，他身上依然持有那把枪。他的手腕和前臂上有着一周前的抓痕，但贝尔坚称那是小狗造成的。弹道学证实贝尔的步枪不是凶器，而且当几名目击者证实他在枪击当天在萨克拉门托看棒球比赛时，他被取消了嫌疑人身份。贝尔只是几名被怀疑是桑迪的年轻男子之一。虽然有些人拥有或能够接触到.22口径火器，但调查人员无法将这些武器中的任何一个与犯罪联系起来。线索十分稀少，而警察掌握的线索又令人困惑。桑迪留下一件绿色军用夹克，领子内侧潦草地写着“罗伯特·考夫曼”这个名字。科尔曼和里德回忆说，桑迪曾说过这件夹克和其余的军装是他偷的。

29
00:30:11.000 --> 00:31:25.000
It was also possible that Kaufman was just another of Sandy's aliases. Either way, the name was a dead end. For their involvement in the killing of Vernon Smith, James Coleman and JC Reid Jr. played a guilty to conspiracy to commit robbery and second-degree murder. They were sent to prison, while the person they alleged had committed the slaying remained on the run. The evening of Wednesday, February 5, 1964, eight months after the murders of Robert Dominguez and Linda Redwoods in Ocean Beach, California. Although Johnny and Joyce Swindle had only been staying in Ocean Beach for a week, they'd already formed a nightly routine. The newlyweds, aged 20 and 19 respectively, did everything together, from washing the dishes to making their bed. Every evening, they left their rented bungalow to take a stroll down to the beach.
考夫曼也可能只是桑迪的另一个化名。无论如何，这个名字是一条死胡同。由于参与谋杀弗农·史密斯，詹姆斯·科尔曼和J·C·里德二世对谋杀阴谋和二级谋杀罪名认罪。他们被送进监狱，而他们指控实施谋杀的人仍然在逃。1964年2月5日星期三傍晚，加利福尼亚州海洋海滩，罗伯特·多明格斯和琳达·雷德伍德谋杀案发生八个月后。尽管强尼和乔伊斯·斯温德尔在海洋海滩只呆了一个星期，但他们已经形成了一套夜间惯例。这对新婚夫妇分别20岁和19岁，做什么都在一起，从洗碗到铺床。每天晚上，他们都会离开租来的平房，散步去海滩。

30
00:31:25.000 --> 00:32:38.000
The night of February 5 was no different, except for a brief visit to a pharmacy where Johnny purchased a red heart-shaped box of candy for his wife. Valentine's Day was more than a week away, but it didn't matter. The childhood sweethearts had been on Cloud 9 since their wedding three weeks earlier. The couple continued their usual walk, which ended nine blocks from their home at the beach front. Joyce in particular loved the ocean. It fascinated her, and Johnny couldn't keep her away. During the day, Ocean Beach foreshore was a hive of activity. Tourists and fishermen lined its pier as swimmers took to the surf below. Just left of the pier at the foot of Narragansett Avenue was a wide concrete patio that provided uninterrupted views of the ocean. It was the perfect spot to observe the sunset. By late evening, most beachgoers had retreated like the tide, leaving the area peaceful and private.
2月5日的夜晚也没有什么不同，只是去了一趟药店，强尼在那里为妻子买了一盒红色的心形糖果。情人节还有一周多才到，但这并不重要。这对青梅竹马自三周前结婚以来就一直沉浸在九霄云上。这对夫妇继续他们通常的散步，散步在距离他们家九个街区的海滨结束。乔伊斯尤其喜欢大海。它令她着迷，强尼无法阻止她靠近。白天，海洋海滩前滨是一个充满活力的活动中心。游客和渔民排成一队在防波堤上，而游泳者则下到下方的海浪中。防波堤左侧、纳拉甘西特大道脚下是一个宽阔的混凝土露台，可以一览无遗地欣赏海景。这里是观赏日落的绝佳地点。到了深夜，大多数海滩游客像潮水一样退去，留下了宁静和私密的空间。

31
00:32:38.000 --> 00:33:35.000
Placing the candy box on the retaining wall framing the water, Johnny and Joyce snuggled together, oblivious to anyone but each other. All of a sudden, Johnny was struck in the back by something small but powerful. He barely had time to register the accompanying pain before Joyce collapsed into his arms. She too had been hit in the upper back. Quickly realizing that they were being shot at, Johnny turned his body into the line of fire trying to shield his wife from the barrage. His pained cries of no, no, carried up the cliffside to the apartment buildings above. Johnny's left thigh was hit and another bullet struck the right side of his head. A bullet pierced Joyce's left arm.
强尼把糖果盒放在构成水景框架的挡土墙上，两人依偎在一起，除了彼此，对外面的世界一无所知。突然，强尼的背部被一个体积小但威力强大的东西击中了。他几乎没有时间意识到随之而来的痛苦，乔伊斯就瘫倒在他的怀里。她也被击中了上背部。很快意识到他们正遭到枪击，强尼将身体转向火线，试图保护妻子免受弹雨袭击。他痛苦的“不，不”的喊声传到了悬崖上方的公寓楼里。强尼的左大腿中弹，另一颗子弹击中了头部右侧。一颗子弹穿透了乔伊斯的左臂。

32
00:33:35.000 --> 00:34:41.000
Exposed and unable to see their assailant in the dark, the couple crumpled helplessly to the ground. With his victims immobilized, the shooter eased down the rocky cliff face to the patio below. Joyce was facedown when he marched up and shot her at point blank range in the back of the head. Then he turned towards Johnny who had collapsed against the retaining wall and fired a bullet into his left ear. After rummaging through Johnny's pockets and taking whatever he could find, the killer then fled the scene. A short while later, Ocean Beach local Edward Nelson descended the steps that led to the patio overlooking the sea. Spotting something on the ground ahead, Edward raised his flashlight, illuminating two bodies piled on top of one another. Edward suspected he had stumbled across a pair of drunk lovers who had passed out together.
由于暴露在外且在黑暗中看不到袭击者，这对夫妇无助地瘫倒在地上。由于受害者失去了行动能力，枪手从岩石悬崖面上轻松走下来，来到下方的露台。当他大步走过去并在近距离朝乔伊斯的后脑勺开枪时，她正脸朝下趴着。然后他转向靠在挡土墙上瘫倒的强尼，向他的左耳开了一枪。在翻找强尼的口袋并拿走他能找到的一切后，凶手逃离了现场。不久之后，海洋海滩当地人爱德华·纳尔逊走下通往俯瞰大海露台的台阶。爱德华发现前方地上有什么东西，便举起手电筒，照亮了叠在一起的两具尸体。爱德华怀疑自己偶然遇到了一对一起昏迷过去的醉酒恋人。

